From 0a474dbbe47d428382769835ab7b330e8a12c995 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Danylo Piliaiev <dpiliaiev@igalia.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:10:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tu: Emit pending flushes when ending a command buffer in a
 s/r chain

Flush bits emitted before a S/R chain that is split between several
command buffers are lost. Because flushes recorded before
vkCmdBeginRendering() were left in the original command buffer's pending
flush bits and never emitted.
Flush those bits at tu_EndCommandBuffer.

Fixes "Mortal Shell 2"

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Danylo Piliaiev <dpiliaiev@igalia.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45985>
(cherry picked from commit 8a494f248a708673dad59b149132a700d07f8eb1)
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
index 97dead60f9e..86acda2b893 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
@@ -5467,7 +5467,12 @@ tu_EndCommandBuffer(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer)
    if (cmd_buffer->state.pass) {
       tu_clean_all_pending(&cmd_buffer->state.renderpass_cache);
       tu_emit_cache_flush_renderpass<CHIP>(cmd_buffer);
-   } else {
+   }
+
+   /* A suspended chain is rendered after cs, so in order to not lose the flushes - do them here. */
+   if (!cmd_buffer->state.pass ||
+       cmd_buffer->state.suspend_resume == SR_IN_CHAIN ||
+       cmd_buffer->state.suspend_resume == SR_IN_CHAIN_AFTER_PRE_CHAIN) {
       tu_clean_all_pending(&cmd_buffer->state.cache);
       cmd_buffer->state.cache.flush_bits |=
          TU_CMD_FLAG_CCU_CLEAN_COLOR |
